{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.ExplicitCentralIdempotent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.ExplicitCentralIdempotent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.explicit_central_idempotent_two_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.explicit_central_idempotent_two_two","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/explicit-central-idempotent.lean#L73-L98","doc":"Computability witness for small `n`: the (2,2) self-conjugate\ncell of `H_4(q)` is the Bring-figure-8 cell, witnessed in\n`conj:bring-figure-eight-depth-2-witness`. The `e_{(2,2)}`\nformula is concrete and finite (sum over 2 SYTs × product\nover 4 boxes × Lagrange factor).\n\n**Conditional, exactly as its parent is** (AGENTS.md §3b-cond\nitem 2). This was previously an `example` with no binders, which\nstated the `(2,2)` idempotency *unconditionally* while proving it\nfrom `explicit_central_idempotent_via_murphy` — a conditional\ntheorem. Lean refused it (`failed to synthesize\nExplicitCentralIdempotentConjecture q`), which is the elaborator\ncatching precisely the smuggling this repo's §3b-cond rules\nforbid: a specialisation does not discharge the hypothesis its\ngeneral form carries. Naming it also makes it citable, which an\nanonymous `example` was not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.explicit_central_idempotent_via_murphy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ExplicitCentralIdempotent.explicit_central_idempotent_via_murphy","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/explicit-central-idempotent.lean#L37-L71","doc":"**Theorem (`prop:explicit-central-idempotent`).** The central\nprimitive idempotent `e_λ` for partition `λ ⊢ n` is given by\n\n  e_λ = ∑_{T ∈ SYT(λ)} ∏_{k=1}^{n} ∏_{□ ∈ λ, □ ≠ T(k)}\n          (J_k - c(□; q)) / (c(T(k); q) - c(□; q))\n\nand satisfies:\n\n- Sum-to-identity:    `∑_λ e_λ = 1`\n- Orthogonality:      `e_λ * e_μ = δ_{λμ} * e_λ`\n- Self-adjointness:   for self-conjugate `λ = λ'`,\n                      `star (e_λ) = e_λ`\n- Bar-pairing:        for chiral pair `λ ≠ λ'`,\n                      `star (e_λ) = e_{λ'}`\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:explicit-central-idempotent","label":"prop:explicit-central-idempotent","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/explicit-central-idempotent.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}